<title>AUSTRIA: OPEC SESSION TO DISCUSS OUTPUT, QUOTAS - DELEGATE.</title>
<headline>OPEC SESSION TO DISCUSS OUTPUT, QUOTAS - DELEGATE.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC's closed session, set to start at 1500 GMT, will discuss production and quotas, a delegate told reporters.  </p>
<p>Ministers were starting to gather for the &quot;consultative&quot; session in the hotel suite of the OPEC President Abdullah Salem al-Badri, the Libyan oil minister.</p>
<p>Indonesia's Ida Bagus Sudjana told reporters on his way to the suite that the meeting was &quot;to do with the quotas and the problem we face&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
